NeuralOps Nexus — Licence
=========================

This repository holds two different things, under two different terms:
the installer files you are looking at, and the NeuralOps Nexus software
they install.


1. The installer files in this repository
-----------------------------------------

The files in this repository — install.sh, the `neuralops` command,
docker-compose.neuralops.yaml, the catalog and the bundled configuration
— are Copyright (c) 2026 Noaman Faisal, and are licensed under the MIT
License (the full text is at the end of this file). You may read, copy,
change and redistribute these files freely.


2. The NeuralOps Nexus software (what the installer installs)
-------------------------------------------------------------

NeuralOps Nexus itself ships as a compiled Docker image
(`noamanfaisal/neuralops` on Docker Hub). The image is NOT covered by
the MIT License above, and it is not open source. Its terms, in plain
words:

  a. Free to self-host. You may download and run NeuralOps Nexus on
     your own servers — for yourself, your team or your company,
     commercial use included — free of charge.

  b. No competing hosted service. You may not offer NeuralOps Nexus to
     third parties as a hosted or managed service.

  c. Keep it intact. You may not remove or circumvent licence-key or
     feature-gating functionality, and you may not remove or alter the
     software's notices.

  d. Source code. The source code is not public yet. We plan to publish
     it under a source-available licence as the project grows.

  e. No warranty. The software is provided "as is", without warranty of
     any kind, express or implied. To the maximum extent permitted by
     law, the author is not liable for any damages arising from its
     use.

Separate projects: our MCP servers contextgraph
(https://github.com/mapax-io/contextgraph) and csv-mcp are open source
under their own Apache-2.0 licences; those licences, not this file,
govern them. Third-party components inside the image (PostgreSQL,
Redis, Centrifugo and others) remain under their own licences.

Questions: info@neuralopsnexus.ai


